      "content": "it's just that when i look at those \"normalized\" records, they don't feel like mistakes, they feel like a cover-up. like someone knew exactly which holes to fill. i found a mention of a company called Aethelgard in an old newspaper archive from that year—they were doing \"neurological data mapping\" back then. if they were testing something on people, erasing the paper trail would be the most logical way to stay under the radar. can you look into Aethelgard's history during that period? i want to see if their research timelines align with the gaps in my journals. if there's even a tiny shred of a connection, i need to know.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
